# Change Context Tracking

After every substantive code change in this repository, append an entry to
`CHANGELOG.md` at the project root. This is the project's persistent memory
of WHY changes were made, not just WHAT changed.

## When to Add an Entry

Add an entry when you:

- Modify business logic in `server.js` (formulas, contracts, endpoints).
- Change UI behaviour or data flow in `public/script.js` / `public/index.html`.
- Alter project configuration (`package.json`, `.replit`, scripts).
- Add or remove files, dependencies, or rules.

Skip the entry only for pure formatting, typo fixes, or trivial doc edits.

## Entry Format

Use the "Keep a Changelog" style with reverse-chronological order. Entries
are written in English; user-visible product changes may also be mirrored
into the Russian `README.md` if relevant.

```
## [Unreleased] - YYYY-MM-DD

### Added
- Short description of new capability and the reason it was needed.

### Changed
- File(s) touched + one-line rationale (the "why", not the diff).

### Fixed
- Bug description, root cause, and fix in one sentence.

### Removed
- What was removed and why it was safe to remove.
```

## Workflow

1. Make the code change first.
2. Read the current top of `CHANGELOG.md`.
3. Append an entry under today's date in `[Unreleased]`. If today's section
   already exists, extend it instead of duplicating.
4. Reference touched files with backticks (e.g. `` `server.js` ``).
5. Keep each bullet under ~120 characters and focused on intent.

Never delete or rewrite historical entries — only append.
